    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "barchart",
      "title": "Signal frequency breakdown",
      "description": "Count of gateway_output turns by pattern signal fired (90d, full history, top 20). Caveat: the recall-cue detector sometimes writes the raw matched user-text verbatim into the signals array instead of a canonical label (e.g. \"Refresh my memory\", \"Going back to earlier\") -- these are one-off strings, not real signal categories, and inflate the apparent diversity of this breakdown. recall_cue_reclassified (5 occurrences) is the canonical marker for those turns; the echoed-text entries are an instrumentation bug, out of scope to fix here.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
